  "articleBody": "After a storm hits Allen, it's natural to want to fix things fast, but rushing can lead to some costly mistakes. Here are a few common missteps homeowners make and how to steer clear of them. One frequent mistake is assuming your roof is fine because you don't see any interior leaks. Hail or wind damage often isn't immediately visible from the ground and can take time to manifest as leaks, so always get a professional to check it out.\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid\n\nNot documenting damage promptly — Snap photos and videos of everything before any cleanup or repairs. This evidence is crucial for insurance claims and helps paint a clear picture of the storm's impact.\n\nStarting permanent repairs before an inspection — While temporary measures are okay to prevent further damage, hold off on full repairs until a professional inspection and documentation are complete. This ensures all damage is assessed properly for your records or insurance.\n\nOnly relying on ground-level observations — Many types of storm damage, like lifted shingles or subtle hail dents, are impossible to spot from the ground. A trained eye on the roof can identify issues you'd never see, preventing bigger problems later.\n\nFailing to distinguish new storm damage from pre-existing wear — An expert inspector can differentiate between recent storm damage and older wear and tear, which is important for accurate insurance claims and repair decisions. Without this distinction, you might not get the coverage you deserve.\n\nAllowing unqualified people onto the roof — Walking an unsafe roof is dangerous, especially if it's unstable or covered in debris. Always leave roof access to qualified professionals who have the right safety equipment and training. This protects both them and your property.\n\nFor honest guidance and a thorough assessment of your storm damage in Allen, reach out to Discounted Roofing Co. today.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}